## Original Content
Après la mort de la figure emblématique de la country, de nombreuses personnalités saluent la mémoire de la chanteuse, à l’image de Bill Clinton, Mick Jagger, Julia Roberts, Jeff Bezos ou encore Tim Cook.

## Summary
Dolly Parton, an iconic country singer, has died. Donald Trump has ordered flags to be flown at half-staff in her honor. Many celebrities and personalities have paid tribute, showing unified emotion across a divided America.

## Key Points
- Dolly Parton, a legendary country music figure, has passed away.
- Donald Trump ordered flags to be at half-staff to honor her.
- Prominent individuals like Bill Clinton, Mick Jagger, and others expressed condolences.
- The event sparked a moment of unity in a typically divided America.


